            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi! Glad you like 'mini.files'!\r\n\r\nThe `MiniFiles.open()` function takes [arguments](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ebc8cb0c1f73ee6c53e0560957a37a2307a70f98/doc/mini-files.txt#L649-L657) which [can be used in different ways](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ebc8cb0c1f73ee6c53e0560957a37a2307a70f98/doc/mini-files.txt#L635-L646).\r\n\r\nFor described case it seems that using `MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))` (which opens directory of current file in a last used state with focus on that file) instead of plain `MiniFiles.open()`.",
