        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You might want to check to make sure `buftype ~= \"nofile\"` so you don't get an error if you use your mapping while in a buffer that doesn't have a real file associated with it. For example, if I use my mapping while on MiniStarter screen, the buftype is \"nofile\", but  the buffer name looks like a path that is not a real file, so I'd get an error if I didn't add this check:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nM.minifiles_open_buffer_path = function()\r\n  local path = vim.bo.buftype ~= \"nofile\" and vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0) or nil\r\n  MiniFiles.open(path)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n",
